{"name":"In the Twilight","hex":"#84838e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twilight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft light in the sky seen before the rising and (especially) after the setting of the sun, occasioned by the illumination of the earth’s atmosphere by the direct rays of the sun and their reflection on the earth.","The time when said light is visible; the period between daylight and darkness."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or resembling twilight; faintly illuminated; obscure.","Synonym of mesopelagic (“Describing the pelagic zone of the ocean between the photic epipelagic and the aphotic bathypelagic zones, characterized by very minimal light.”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight"}],"entries":[{"title":"In the Twilight","blocks":[{"text":"In the Twilight is a 1915 American silent short drama film directed by Tom Ricketts. The film stars Perry Banks, Charlotte Burton, Reaves Eason, David Lythgoe, Louise Lester, Vivian Rich, and Harry Van Meter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Twilight","wikidata":"Q6013027"},{"title":"Twilight","blocks":[{"text":"Twilight is daylight illumination produced by diffuse sky radiation when the Sun is below the horizon as sunlight from the upper atmosphere is scattered in a way that illuminates both the Earth's lower atmosphere and also the Earth's surface. Twilight also may be any period when this illumination occurs, including dawn and dusk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Twilight_description_full_day.svg/330px-Twilight_description_full_day.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight","wikidata":"Q164160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Twilight_December_30%2C_2016.jpg/500px-Twilight_December_30%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut